        "original_id": "7ed74c6d-206f-51c9-a6a3-2929eb60afa1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Cleveland Thyagaraja Festival\n- People: Tyagaraja\n- Places: Cleveland, Ohio\n- Concepts: Carnatic music, South Indian classical music and dance, Indian classical music\n\nFacts:\n- Tyagaraja, also known as Kakarla Tyagabrahmam, Saint Tyagaraja, and Tyāgayya in Telugu, was born on 4 May 1767 and died on 6 January 1847.\n- Tyagaraja was one of the greatest composers of Carnatic music, a form of Indian classical music.\n- The Cleveland Thyagaraja Festival is a 12-day festival of South Indian classical music and dance in Cleveland, Ohio.\n- The Cleveland Thyagaraja Festival is held each year around Easter weekend.",
